<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanbo Steel to be auctioned July 8.</title>
<headline>Hanbo Steel to be auctioned July 8.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea First Bank, the main creditor bank to failed Hanbo Steel Co, said on Friday it would hold an open auction on July 8 to sell Hanbo on behalf of all creditor banks.  </p>
<p>Hanbo's creditors had taken over 26.5 percent, or 5.71 million of Hanbo shares from the company's founder Chung Tae-soo and his family after Hanbo defaulted on debt payments.</p>
<p>The steelmaker's failure has rocked the country's financial markets and uncovered a huge loans-for-kickbacks scandal, leading to the arrests of senior politicians and top bankers.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
